     3	// Adapted from X0nk Bliss Stable lib/nether_fog.glsl, retrieved 2026-09-10.
     4	// Original noise layout; Astra exposure uses lower plume/ceiling density.
     5	//
     6	// This volume is composited over the plain nether fog in program/scene.glsl as
     7	//   result = result * volume.a + volume.rgb
     8	// which is the single-scattering form: the volume attenuates what is behind it and
     9	// adds its own in-scattered light exactly once. Do not fold the plain-fog term in
    10	// here as well, or the medium absorbs twice.
    11	//
    12	// Astra density scale. The reference runs this march over a longer distance with more
    13	// samples; Astra keeps 16 samples and shortens the march, so the per-step densities
    14	// are dialled down to keep the plumes readable instead of blanketing the view.

